nes","dish/bistro-agnes"],["Bistro Jeanty","dish/bistro-jeanty"]]}]},"dish/ghonghi":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/ghonghi","n":"Ghonghi","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Nepalese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Ghonghi is a Nepalese freshwater snail dish prepared by the Tharu and Madheshi people of southern Nepal. It is eaten by sucking the snail from its shell and is found throughout the Madhesh Province and Terai districts of other states. It is also popular among Rajbanshi, Dhimals, Santhal and Danuwar people of Terai."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-ghonghi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghonghi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Nepalese cuisine","cuisine/nepalese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Flaxseed","ingredient/flaxseed"],["Freshwater snail","ingredient/freshwater-snail"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Gundruk","ref":"site/thegundruk-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thegundruk.com","note":"Blog dedicated to Nepali recipes and food culture.","url":"https://thegundruk.com","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Nepalese cuisine","links":[["Annapurna Cafe","dish/annapurna-cafe"],["Dhikri","dish/dhikri"],["Mokthuk","dish/mokthuk"],["Momo (food)","dish/momo-food"],["Sel roti","dish/sel-roti"],["Sichuan pepper","dish/sichuan-pepper"],["Sohari","dish/sohari"],["Thali","dish/thali"]]}]},"ingredient/cornstarch":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/cornstarch","n":"Cornstarch","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 3 dishes across 3 cuisines","intro":[["Corn starch or cornstarch (American English), cornflour (British English) is the starch powder derived from corn grain. The starch is obtained from the endosperm of the kernel."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-cornstarch"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornstarch"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked wit